+<div class="entry status-kept" id="c033">
+    <div class="entry-head">
+      <span class="entry-id">#033 &middot; KEPT</span>
+      <span class="entry-status">KEPT</span>
+    </div>
+    <h3>The first 40M Streamflow lock matured on August 18. The full scheduled allocation is re-locked for two additional years, with both contracts and both transactions preserved.</h3>
+    <div class="meta">
+      <span>Matured 2026-08-18 &middot; re-locked 2026-08-28</span>
+      <span>Affected: /treasury &middot; commitment #002</span>
+    </div>
+    <div class="body">
+      <p><strong>What matured.</strong> The original Lock 3 held <strong>40,000,000 $GFOF</strong> under Streamflow metadata account <a href="https://app.streamflow.finance/contract/solana/mainnet/7HKRtFyeFAmxuSzXrZ8rayDYGBwSJZMgrn8Xna6hqg7k" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--cyan);text-decoration:underline;word-break:break-all">7HKRtFyeFAmxuSzXrZ8rayDYGBwSJZMgrn8Xna6hqg7k</a>. Its full cliff was 2026-08-18 05:00 UTC. Streamflow auto-claimed the 40M to the disclosed recipient wallet in <a href="https://solscan.io/tx/54jUeZMPsa3gsMgocppv8iLhv89gsUrRTgeFAFLjpQ2ioEiatvoXiTyxesie3sLr1fkEHSB2uZoWezoEaRsKBiNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--cyan);text-decoration:underline;word-break:break-all">transaction 54jUeZMP&hellip;KBiNG</a> at 2026-08-18 05:00:15 UTC.</p>
+      <p><strong>What was done.</strong> On 2026-08-28, the same recipient wallet created a new Streamflow contract and placed the full <strong>40,000,000 $GFOF scheduled allocation</strong> under a new full cliff of <strong>2028-08-18 05:00 UTC</strong>. Active metadata account: <a href="https://app.streamflow.finance/contract/solana/mainnet/6VjeLZ27NKpTs7n2rVj5pXPQaUrRFFjdk7AV2FwbzojS" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--cyan);text-decoration:underline;word-break:break-all">6VjeLZ27NKpTs7n2rVj5pXPQaUrRFFjdk7AV2FwbzojS</a>. Creation transaction: <a href="https://solscan.io/tx/5zr6i6atKvtHi6dPQqTo9du8dBcoHNfqSSU3nubGoQF8PTh876Q8yS5hr9cxjiUDtGxoxU2qUyA8ACCU5nKwjqXD" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--cyan);text-decoration:underline;word-break:break-all">5zr6i6at&hellip;KwjqXD</a>.</p>
+      <p><strong>Why the new escrow can show 40.2M.</strong> The creation transaction transferred 40,200,000 $GFOF into the Streamflow escrow because the transaction logs include a 200,000-token Streamflow fee. The contract metadata records <strong>40,000,000 $GFOF as the net scheduled deposit</strong>. The treasury page therefore counts the scheduled 40M allocation, not the platform fee, when computing the locked-supply total.</p>
+      <p><strong>What this means for the total.</strong> The active scheduled lock set remains <strong>130,000,000 $GFOF &mdash; 13% of total supply &mdash; across four active Streamflow contracts</strong>: 30M, 30M, the re-locked 40M, and 30M. The expired predecessor is retained as lineage rather than erased or presented as active.</p>
+      <p><strong>Status:</strong> <a href="#c002" style="color:var(--cyan);text-decoration:underline">Commitment #002</a> is marked KEPT. The full first-maturity allocation was re-locked; no amount from that 40M scheduled allocation was removed from the re-lock. This entry records the ten-day interval between maturity and the new contract rather than implying the extension happened automatically on August 18.</p>
+    </div>
+  </div>
